# Version 1 of what a forge adapter answers Porelo about one pull request's review: its facts, the open pull request
# from a branch, its whole conversation one page at a time, one released result written and one thread resolved. Nothing of a forge's own
# format crosses: a conversation and a submission are review profile 2 documents. No method reaches a verdict; the
# adapter reads what the forge says and writes what Porelo released, and decides nothing.
# The token comes with each call over the owner-only socket, lent for that call alone; an adapter keeps no secret of
# its own, never logs the token and never puts it in an error. One adapter executable serves this interface and
# org.fuin.porelo.Build2 on one socket; one that reads no review answers neither this interface nor its Describe.
# api is the forge's REST base URL, "" for the forge's public one, as Build2's Target says.
interface org.fuin.porelo.Review1

# Which forge, and which version of this contract the adapter speaks; Porelo refuses any version but 1.
method Describe() -> (protocolVersion: int, forge: string)

# A pull request's facts, by its https address. head is the commit reviewed, for a merged one the head that merged;
# base the base branch's commit and mergeBase the merge base of the two, each a full commit id. mergeCommit and
# mergedHead (the branch the merge commit went onto) are given exactly when merged. decidedAt is when the forge
# merged or closed it, an RFC 3339 time in UTC ending in Z (the forge's merged_at for merged, its closed_at for
# closed), given exactly when merged or closed. approved is the forge's observed verdict at head, read only, never
# one this adapter reaches. repository is the https address of the repository the head is read from. account is
# the forge account the given token stands for (for GitHub what GET /user answers), absent only when the forge
# does not say.
method PullRequest(api: string, token: string, url: string)
    -> (repository: string, head: string, base: string, mergeBase: string, state: (open, merged, closed),
        approved: bool, mergeCommit: ?string, mergedHead: ?string, decidedAt: ?string, account: ?ForgeAccount)

# An account at the forge, bounded as review profile 2 bounds porelo/forgeAccountId and porelo/forgeAccountName:
# id is the forge's id of the account, which a renamed account keeps, 1 to 64 characters (for GitHub its numeric id
# as a decimal string); login its name as shown, 1 to 256 characters. Neither holds a control character.
type ForgeAccount (id: string, login: string)

# The open pull request from a branch of the repository upstream names, as the project file names it; absent when
# none is open. Read only: it opens none.
method PullRequestOf(api: string, token: string, upstream: string, branch: string) -> (url: ?string)

# One page of a pull request's whole conversation: document is one profile 2 document of porelo/documentKind page,
# which states its own completeness, at most 100 results and 1 MiB. cursor is absent for the first page; the answer's
# cursor is absent after the last one.
method Comments(api: string, token: string, url: string, cursor: ?string)
    -> (document: string, cursor: ?string)

# Writes one released result: document is one profile 2 submission of exactly one result. thread is the thread
# answered, or the id of the new thread's root. A thread id is the forge's native id as a decimal string; for GitHub
# its root comment's REST id.
method Post(api: string, token: string, url: string, document: string) -> (thread: string)

# Marks one thread of the pull request resolved, as the account the token stands for. thread is the thread's id as
# Comments and Post give it. A thread the forge already shows resolved is answered as done, so a second call for
# the same thread changes nothing. A forge that cannot resolve a thread answers ResolveUnsupported and writes
# nothing; a thread the pull request does not hold is NoSuchThread.
method Resolve(api: string, token: string, url: string, thread: string) -> ()

# The forge limits how often it is asked; retryAfter is in seconds, 0 when it did not say.
error RateLimited(retryAfter: int)

# The forge refused the token: expired, revoked, wrong, or without the scope it needs.
error CredentialRefused()

# The forge knows no pull request at that address, or the token may not see it.
error NoSuchPullRequest()

# A submission answers a thread the pull request does not hold.
error NoSuchThread()

# The forge did not answer, or answered something that is not an answer.
error Unreachable()

# A Post or Resolve was sent and no answer says whether it was written. Porelo never sends a Post again. It
# sends a Resolve again only after the pull request's conversation, read anew, still shows the thread open.
error WriteOutcomeUnknown()

# The forge has no way to mark a thread resolved; the thread stays open.
error ResolveUnsupported()

# What the forge holds or was asked to write is something profile 2 cannot carry, such as a general or a file
# comment; field names the first point of it.
error NotInProfile(field: string)

# The adapter itself failed; message says why, never the token.
error Failed(message: string)
